# Local MLB Numerology email previews
public/data/mlb/numerology/email-preview.html

# CFB Model V2 browser artifact (WU7A). public/data/nfl, public/data/pga,
# and public/data/mlb (see the MLB local-preview exception a few lines up)
# establish the repo convention: tracked public/data output is NOT broadly
# ignored — at most specific local-only files are excepted. Mirror that
# exactly here rather than blanket-ignoring the directory (a blanket
# ignore makes `git add public/data/cfb/v2/shadow-projections.json` FAIL
# outright — plain `git add` on an ignored path is a no-op error, not a
# silent success — forcing a workflow to either use `-f`, surprising and
# easy to leave un-tested, or silently never publish anything). Ignore
# everything else that might land in this directory (e.g. a stray local
# dev/test run's output under a different filename), but the one real
# deployment artifact stays a normal tracked path, committed only by the
# scheduled cfb-v2-shadow-refresh.yml workflow.
public/data/cfb/v2/*
!public/data/cfb/v2/shadow-projections.json
public/data/mlb/numerology/email-preview.txt
